hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20929","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyub from Muhammad who said: Al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari was appointed over Khurasan. He said: Imran ibn Husayn longed for him until it was said to him: O Abu Nujayd, shall we call him for you. He said: No. So Imran ibn Husayn stood and met him among the people. He said: Do you remember the day the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No obedience to a created being in disobedience of Allah. He said: Yes. Imran said: Allah is Greatest."
"20930","Bahz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Humayd, meaning Ibn Hilal, narrated to us from Abdullah ibn al-Samit who said: Ziyad wanted to send Imran ibn Husayn over Khurasan, but he refused them. His companions said to him: Did you leave Khurasan to be over it. He said: By Allah, it would not please me to pray in its heat while you pray in its cold. I fear when I am at the throats of the enemy a letter comes to me from Ziyad, then if I proceed I perish, and if I return my neck will be struck. He said: So he wanted al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari for it. He said: He submitted to his order. He said: Imran said: Is there anyone to call al-Hakam for me. He said: The messenger went. He said: Al-Hakam came to him. He said: He entered upon him. He said: Imran said to al-Hakam: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No obedience to anyone in disobedience of Allah, blessed and exalted. He said: Yes. Imran said: Praise be to Allah, or Allah is Greatest."
"20931","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us from Abu Hajib from a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Banu Ghifar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to perform ablution from the leftover purification water of a woman."
"20932","Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, narrated to us, Hisham informed us from Muhammad who said: A man came to Imran ibn Husayn while we were with him and said: Al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari has been appointed over Khurasan, so Imran longed for him until a man of the people said to him: Shall we call him for you. He said to him: No. Then Imran stood and met him among the people, and Imran said: You have been given a great matter of the Muslims affairs, then he commanded him and forbade him and admonished him, then said: Do you remember the day the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No obedience to a created being in disobedience of Allah, blessed and exalted. Al-Hakam said: Yes. Imran said: Allah is Greatest."
"20933","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal who said: I heard Abu Hajib narrating from al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to perform ablution from the leftover ablution water of a woman."
"20934","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, he said: I asked Muhammad about the hadith of Imran ibn Husayn. He said: I was told that Imran ibn Husayn said to al-Hakam al-Ghifari, both of them from the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Do you know the day the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No obedience in disobedience of Allah, blessed and exalted. He said: Yes. Imran said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest."
"20935","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Yunus and Humayd informed us from al-Hasan that Ziyad appointed al-Hakam al-Ghifari over an army, so Imran ibn Husayn came to him and met him among the people and said: Do you know why I came to you. He said to him: Why. He said: Do you remember the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to the man to whom his commander said: Fall into the fire, so he was reached and hesitated, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was informed of that and said: Had he fallen into it they would both have entered the Fire together. No obedience in disobedience of Allah, blessed and exalted. He said: Yes. He said: I only wanted to remind you of this hadith."
"20936","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Habib ibn Abdullah al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari who said: I and my brother Rafi ibn Amr entered upon the Commander of the Faithful Umar ibn al-Khattab, I being dyed with henna and my brother dyed with yellow. Umar ibn al-Khattab said to me: This is the dye of Islam, and said to my brother Rafi: This is the dye of faith."
"20937","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us from more than one, among them Ayyub from Ibn Sirin that Ziyad appointed al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari, so Imran ibn Husayn said: I wish I meet him before he leaves. He said: He met him and Imran said to him: Do you not know, or did you not hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No obedience to anyone in disobedience of Allah, blessed and exalted. He said: Yes. He said: That is what I wanted to say to you."
